cl compiles this case against its own STL and cxx1 against include/, so each defines the other library's members (cl's std::_Allocate, bad_array_new_length, its <lambda_...> helpers; cxx1's basic_string, logic_error) - two libraries, not two manglings. The catchable type's name carries the thrown class's size, and Failure holds a std::string: 48 bytes with include/'s string, 40 with cl's STL - the library's layout, not the ABI's. cxx1 emits an implicit or local member, or a vbase destructor ??_D, that cl inlines at its one use and so does not emit - the shape virtual-base-diamond.nocl records. Measured by names-vs-cl at rv-I, 2026-11-13.
